      <x>645</x>
      <y>125</y>
      <width>125</width>
      <height>30</height>
      <format>3</format>
      <precision>6</precision>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):FBR_ILK_TH_100MS (FBR_ILK_TH_CH$(CH)_100MS)
Fiber-count interlock threshold, counts. Enter a non-negative integer; scientific notation such as 1e9 is accepted. Written to the FPGA 100ms window threshold.</tooltip>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>ADCWarn</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_WARN_TH</pv_name>
      <x>125</x>
      <y>172</y>
      <width>255</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):ADC_WARN_TH (ADC_ILK_WARN_TH_CH$(CH))

ADC warning level of channel $(CH), as a fraction of the interlock
thresholds of the same channel: 50% (0), 25% (1) or 12.5% (2), default
12.5%. The FPGA compares the calibrated integrals of this channel against
the scaled level and raises warn_signal_&lt;scale&gt;; a warning is only an
indication, it does not trip the interlock.

Written to interlock_threshold.reg0.warning_thd_switch the moment the
selection changes, and shared by all five time scales of this channel
(1 us, 10 us, 100 us, 1 ms, 10 ms) at once. The driver applies no range
check, so only these three enum values are meaningful.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>50%</item>
        <item>25%</item>
        <item>12.5%</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>FBRWarn</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):FBR_WARN_TH</pv_name>
      <x>515</x>
      <y>172</y>
      <width>255</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):FBR_WARN_TH (FBR_ILK_WARN_TH_CH$(CH))

Fiber count warning level of channel $(CH), as a fraction of the interlock
thresholds of the same channel: 50% (0), 25% (1) or 12.5% (2), default
12.5%. The FPGA compares the fiber counts of this channel against the
scaled level and raises warn_signal_&lt;scale&gt;; a warning is only an
indication, it does not trip the interlock.

Written to interlock_threshold.reg0.warning_thd_switch the moment the
selection changes, and shared by all five time scales of this channel
(1 us, 10 us, 100 us, 1 ms, 10 ms) at once. The driver applies no range
check, so only these three enum values are meaningful.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>50%</item>
        <item>25%</item>
        <item>12.5%</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
